   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "A wish about someone else",
     "texto": [
      "To ask something politely of another person, use a wish verb in the **conditional** and the **imperfect subjunctive**:\n\n- **Me gustaría que vinieras** to lunch.\n- **Quisiera que conocieras** my sister.\n- **Preferiría que me avisaras** in advance.\n\nIf the subject is the **same**, use the infinitive: **me gustaría viajar**.\n\nThe imperfect subjunctive is formed from the 3rd person plural of the **preterite**: **hablaron → hablara**, **comieron → comiera**, **vivieron → viviera**. The **-se** form also exists (viniese).\n\nEven if it looks past, here it speaks of the **present or the future**: it is a wish, not a memory."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Imperfect subjunctive",
     "texto": [
      "It is formed from the 3rd person plural of the **preterite**, dropping **-ron** and adding:\n\n- **-ra, -ras, -ra, -ramos, -rais, -ran**: hablara, hablaras, hablara, hablá**ramos**, hablarais, hablaran.\n\nVerbs that are irregular in the preterite keep their stem: vinieron → **viniera**, tuvieron → **tuviera**, hicieron → **hiciera**, fueron → **fuera**, dijeron → **dijera**, pudieron → **pudiera**.\n\nIt is used:\n\n- After a wish in the conditional: **me gustaría que vinieras**.\n- After a wish or request in the past: **quería que vinieras**.\n- With **ojalá** for a hard-to-reach wish: **ojalá pudiera**.\n\nThe **-se** form (viniese) means the same but is used less."
     ],
